{number: 119}
{title: Great King of Glory}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Great King of glory, [F] come,
And with Thy [C] favor [G7] crown
This [C] temple as Thine [F] own,
This [C] people [G7] as Thine [C] own:
Beneath this [F] roof, O [C] deign to [G7] show
How [C] God can [F] dwell with [C] men be-[G7] [C] low.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
Here [C] may Thine ear at-[F] tend
Our [C] humble, [G7] earnest cries,
And [C] grateful praise as-[F] cend,
Like [C] incense, [G7] to the [C] skies:
Here may Thy [F] Word me-[C] lodious [G7] sound,
And [C] spread ce-[F] lestial [C] joys a-[G7] [C] round.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
Here [C] may the list'ning [F] throng
Re-[C] ceive Thy [G7] truth with love,
And [C] converts join the [F] song
Of [C] seraph-[G7] im a-[C] bove:
Till all who [F] go from [C] earth a-[G7] way
Shall [C] join the [F] choir in [C] endless [G7] [C] day.
{end_of_verse}
